add([17,18],'reading question',[14,32],'400–407;863–869','Il n\'faut surtout pas les confondre','For n invertible, μ_n is an étale rank-one Z/n-local system; μ_n(d) is not canonically constant. A primitive-root rescaling uses λ∈(Z/n)×. For smooth relative dimension d, T_X/Y=μ_n^{⊗d}.','The needed unit restriction is an earlier-run scope test. Direction of trivialization matters: ζ↦1 changes by λ^(−d), whereas1↦ζ^⊗d changes by λ^d.','understates','The unit alarm is correct; the written direction μ_n^⊗d→Z/n also raises an inverse-power convention question not noted in N16.')
