add([23,33,34,35],'unproved claim',[20,28,32,34],'522–534;773–777;863–908','Les conditions caractérisent les hom Tr_f','For smooth compactifiable pure-dimensional f:X→Y, n invertible, the trace R^{2d}f!Z/n(d)→Z/n is normalized by base change, transitivity, isomorphisms and P¹ Kummer class; it is an isomorphism when geometric fibres are nonempty connected. Étale relative dimension0 gives summation.','Locally varying dimension uses componentwise twists/shifts. SpecC→SpecR with F3 disproves ordinary connected-fibre sufficiency; geometric is the modern correction.','agrees','The notes correctly preserve existence, uniqueness, twists and the fibre-convention obstruction as distinct obligations.')
